{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-timeagg-soak-month-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.67, step 7f. `scale-county-timeagg-soak-month`: THC at evaporative permeation, fuel vapor venting and fuel leaks under `<aggregateBy key=\"Month\"/>` and `<outputtimestep value=\"Month\"/>`, for the gasoline passenger car and light commercial truck at Washtenaw County SINGLE scale, road types 1 and 4, January and July 2020, both day types, all 24 hours, over a county database that STATES soakActivityFraction (`inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg-soak.esm`: source type 21 every month, 32 January only).\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is PreAggDAY.sql's collapse of the stated hourly rows, `sum(soakActivityFraction x HourWeighting2)` per day type, and PreAggMONTH.sql's of those, `sum(x DayWeighting2)` into the whole week -- DayWeighting2 is not normalised, so the collapsed fraction is about 4.25 and the All Running residual is clamped to 0 -- before TankTemperatureGenerator keeps them (`evap_soakCellWeight`), and TTG-6's all-or-nothing switch: with ANY stated row in the zone it writes none, so the light commercial truck in July has no soak row, no evaporative operating-mode distribution and no output row (PLAN.md §7.3.67).\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to the (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs per (county, month, day) cell, recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "time-aggregation",
      "output-time-step",
      "evaporative"
    ]
  },
